# MASTER BUILD PROMPT — SHUDHI LOGISTICS MANAGEMENT PLATFORM

## 1. Project objective

Build a complete, responsive, interactive web application named **SHUDHI LOGISTICS — Integrated Logistics Operations & Management Platform**.

This is a multi-city logistics management platform for coordinating:

1. First-mile pickup from customers or sub-agents.
2. Mid-mile transportation through APSRTC Logistics.
3. Last-mile delivery through independent local delivery partners.
4. Sub-agent booking management and settlements.
5. Customer communication and shipment tracking.
6. Financial management, collections, transporter payables and operational profitability.
7. WhatsApp-based communication and operational automation.

This must be a functional application with working forms, navigation, data management, role-based access, status transitions, calculations, filters, reports and realistic workflows.

**Do not build a static UI, landing page, or clickable visual prototype with non-functional buttons.**

Use the uploaded `shudhi_logistics_app.tsx` as the reference for the existing Version 1. Preserve useful functionality, improve the architecture, fix bugs and extend the application. Do not blindly copy its limitations.

## 2. Business model and operating structure

SHUDHI Logistics operates as the primary logistics agent.

APSRTC Logistics is the mid-mile transportation provider.

SHUDHI manages:
- Customer acquisition and booking coordination.
- Sub-agent network management.
- First-mile pickup coordination.
- Shipment handover to APSRTC.
- Mid-mile tracking and exception management.
- Destination coordination.
- Last-mile delivery through local delivery partners.
- Customer collections and payment tracking.
- Agent commissions and settlements.
- Local pickup and delivery partner payments.

APSRTC Logistics portal reference:
https://logistics.apsrtconline.in/login

Do not attempt to access or automate this external portal without authorized API access. For the initial build, provide a functional APSRTC simulation with the ability to enter actual transporter references and update tracking manually. Design the integration layer so a genuine API can be connected later.

