## 8. Shipment lifecycle and tracking

Implement a proper shipment state machine.

Use the following statuses:

### Booking
- Pending Approval.
- Approved.
- Rejected.

### First-mile pickup
- Pickup Initiated.
- Out for Pickup.
- Pickup Completed.
- Pickup Failed.
- Handed at Origin HUB.

### Mid-mile transportation
- At Origin HUB.
- Dispatched / On the Way.
- At Transhipment.
- Journey Resumed.
- Reached Destination HUB.
- Unloaded at Destination HUB.

### Last-mile delivery
- At Delivery Facility.
- Delivery Initiated.
- Out for Delivery.
- Delivered.
- Delivery Failed.

### Exceptions
- Exception / Issue.
- Cancelled.
- Returned, if enabled by SHUDHI Admin.

Every status change must:
- Record date and time.
- Record the user who performed the action.
- Record the previous status and new status.
- Allow an optional or mandatory reason depending on the action.
- Appear in the shipment timeline.

Prevent invalid status transitions.

Provide a visual tracking timeline for each shipment.

